{
  "title": "Audit ~100 swallowed-error sites violating the fail-fast rule",
  "description": "Project rule: never fail gracefully, always fail fast. But \
server/ and ramekin-core/ contain ~109 occurrences of \
.unwrap_or_default()/.unwrap_or()/.ok() patterns, many of which silently \
swallow real failures. Concrete example: server/src/api/recipes/export.rs:83 \
does serde_json::from_value(version.ingredients.clone()).unwrap_or_default() — \
a recipe whose stored ingredients JSON fails to deserialize exports with an \
EMPTY ingredient list, no error anywhere. Similar patterns in \
server/src/scraping/steps.rs \
(serde_json::to_value(&output).unwrap_or_default() losing step outputs) and \
api/recipes/list.rs.\n\
\n\
Task: sweep these sites and classify each as (a) legitimately optional (e.g. \
genuinely absent optional field) or (b) swallowed failure — and convert (b) to \
propagate an error. Where intent is genuinely 'continue on failure' (there's a \
TODO at scraping/mod.rs ~line 234 questioning exactly this), make it an \
explicit decision with a tracing::warn! at minimum, or fail the step.\n\
\n\
Grep starting point: `rg 'unwrap_or_default|unwrap_or\\(|\\.ok\\(\\)' \
server/src ramekin-core/src`. Expect this to surface follow-up bugs; file them \
rather than scope-creeping.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "server",
    "ramekin-core",
    "error-handling",
  ],
